@startuml builder-lifecycle-state
' LlingWfstBuilder lifecycle: the exact state machine implemented by
' src/ffi.rs. Open is the only mutable state; build() is the one consuming
' transition; a failed build (no start state) restores Open. Palette:
' docs/diagrams/README.md — lling #FCF3CF, error paths #B71C1C.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #FCF3CF
  BorderColor #9A7D0A
  FontColor #102027
  ArrowColor #607D8B
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #ECEFF1
  BorderColor #455A64
}

title <b>LlingWfstBuilder lifecycle</b>\n<size:11><i>every transition is one lling_wfst_builder_* call; non-OK statuses leave the state unchanged unless shown</i></size>

state "Open\n(graph: Some)" as Open #FCF3CF
state "Consumed\n(graph: None)" as Consumed #FFECB3
state "Built handle\nLlingWfst (immutable)" as Handle #DCEDC8

[*] --> Open : lling_wfst_builder_new(&b) → OK

Open --> Open : reserve_states(n) → OK
Open --> Open : add_state(&s) → OK\nset_start(s) → OK | INVALID_ARGUMENT
Open --> Open : set_final(s, w) / clear_final(s)\n→ OK | INVALID_ARGUMENT
Open --> Open : add_arc(...) → OK | INVALID_ARGUMENT\n(non-tropical weight: NaN or −inf;\nnon-scalar label, presence flag > 1,\nabsent endpoint)
Open --> Open : <color:#B71C1C>build(&w) with no start state\n→ INVALID_ARGUMENT (graph restored)</color>
Open --> Consumed : build(&w) → OK\n(<latex>O(1)</latex> freeze into LlingWfst)
Consumed --> Handle : out_wfst receives the handle
Consumed --> Consumed : any builder call\n→ <color:#B71C1C>CLOSED</color>
Open --> [*] : lling_wfst_builder_free
Consumed --> [*] : lling_wfst_builder_free
Handle --> [*] : lling_wfst_free\n(after releasing exported resources)

note right of Open
  Builder calls are **not** thread-safe:
  one builder belongs to one thread.
  All argument validation happens here —
  the built handle can never contain a
  NaN / −∞ weight or an invalid label.
end note

note bottom of Consumed
  build(&w) failure never destroys caller
  state: precedence is builder-null →
  out-null (builder untouched) → CLOSED →
  no-start (graph restored). Only a
  successful build consumes the builder.
end note

legend right
  |<#FCF3CF> mutable builder state (lling) |
  |<#FFECB3> consumed builder (terminal) |
  |<#DCEDC8> immutable handle / VtResource side |
endlegend
@enduml
